{"name":"Evergreen Field","hex":"#47534f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"evergreen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of plants, especially trees, that do not shed their leaves seasonally.","Continually fresh or self-renewing.\n Being a clause which causes an automatic renewal of a contract unless action is taken.\n Of a document, a piece of software, or a data set: kept continually up to date (as opposed to being published at regular intervals and outdated in the meantime)"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub or tree that does not shed its leaves or needles seasonally.","A conifer tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evergreen"},{"term":"field","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A land area free of woodland, cities, and towns; an area of open country.","The open country near or belonging to a town or city."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To intercept or catch (a ball) and play it.","To be the team catching and throwing the ball, as opposed to hitting it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/field"}],"entries":[{"title":"Evergreen Field","blocks":[{"text":"Evergreen Field, also known as Evergreen Airport, was a public-use airport located five miles (8.0 km) east of the central business district of Vancouver, a city in Clark County, Washington, United States. It was located northeast of the intersection of Southeast Mill Plain Boulevard & Southeast 136th Avenue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Evergreen_Field_Powerline_Warning_Cone.jpg/330px-Evergreen_Field_Powerline_Warning_Cone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evergreen_Field"},{"title":"Evergreen","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, an evergreen is a plant which has foliage that remains green and functional throughout the year. This contrasts with deciduous plants, which lose their foliage completely during the winter or dry season. Consisting of many different species, the unique feature of evergreen plants lends itself to various environments and purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Abies_alba_02.jpg/330px-Abies_alba_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evergreen"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Evergreen_Field_June_2010.jpg/500px-Evergreen_Field_June_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Evergreen_Field_June_2010.jpg/1280px-Evergreen_Field_June_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Evergreen_Field_June_2010.jpg/500px-Evergreen_Field_June_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The open field where Evergreen Field was located.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEvergreen_Field_June_2010.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/%CE%95%CE%B8%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%94%CF%81%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%A3%CE%B1%CE%BC%CE%B1%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.jpg/500px-%CE%95%CE%B8%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%94%CF%81%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%A3%CE%B1%CE%BC%CE%B1%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/%CE%95%CE%B8%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%94%CF%81%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%A3%CE%B1%CE%BC%CE%B1%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.jpg/1280px-%CE%95%CE%B8%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%94%CF%81%CF%85%CE%BC%CF%8C%CF%82_%CE%A3%CE%B1%CE%BC%CE%B1%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%AC%CF%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/